{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-spain-people-culture-history-and-food/audio/main-e2eb141b4b43.mp3","durationSec":240.84,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.16,"text":"Spain is in the south-west of Europe."},{"start":2.98,"end":5.2,"text":"Many people in Spain live in big cities."},{"start":5.2,"end":8.24,"text":"Madrid is the capital and the biggest city."},{"start":8.24,"end":10.68,"text":"Barcelona is another very big city."},{"start":11.48,"end":13.48,"text":"Other people live on islands in the sea."},{"start":13.9,"end":16.84,"text":"So daily life can look very different from place to place."},{"start":17.56,"end":19.12,"text":"Work days can feel different too."},{"start":20.12,"end":24.08,"text":"In the past, many shops and businesses closed in the middle of the day."},{"start":24.54,"end":26.66,"text":"They often closed for two or three hours."},{"start":27.24,"end":29.82,"text":"This gave people time for a long lunch at home."},{"start":29.82,"end":33.06,"text":"Family and friends are an important part of the day."},{"start":34.74,"end":38.46,"text":"A long time ago, Muslim rulers governed a big part of Spain."},{"start":39.24,"end":41.84,"text":"People call these lands Al-Andalus."},{"start":41.84,"end":46.46,"text":"Al-Andalus lasted from 711 to 1492."},{"start":47,"end":48.84,"text":"That is almost 800 years."},{"start":50,"end":52.74,"text":"The city of Granada was the last Muslim kingdom."},{"start":53.48,"end":57.54,"text":"In 1492, it was taken by a Christian queen and king."},{"start":58.1,"end":61.78,"text":"The Alhambra in Granada is from the time of Al-Andalus."},{"start":61.78,"end":65.14,"text":"It is an old palace and a strong building that protected the city."},{"start":65.9,"end":67.58,"text":"Today, Spain is very different."},{"start":68.12,"end":70,"text":"People choose their government by voting."},{"start":70.6,"end":72.14,"text":"The country also has a king."},{"start":73.06,"end":74.72,"text":"Spain is part of the European Union."},{"start":75.48,"end":78.22,"text":"Spain has 17 regions with their own governments."},{"start":78.96,"end":80.98,"text":"Each region makes some of its own decisions."},{"start":81.76,"end":83.06,"text":"Andalusia is in the south."},{"start":83.68,"end":85.94,"text":"Catalonia is in the north-east."},{"start":85.94,"end":87.58,"text":"Everyone in Spain learns Spanish."},{"start":88.24,"end":90.1,"text":"It is the language for the whole country."},{"start":90.76,"end":93.36,"text":"But some regions have a second official language."},{"start":93.88,"end":96,"text":"People speak Catalan around Barcelona."},{"start":96.68,"end":99.24,"text":"People speak Galician in the north-west."},{"start":99.24,"end":100.66,"text":"People speak Basque in the north."},{"start":101.64,"end":103.18,"text":"Basque is very different from Spanish."},{"start":103.88,"end":106.52,"text":"It is not related to most other languages in Europe."},{"start":107.26,"end":110.96,"text":"Let’s connect three cities with three famous places."},{"start":111.46,"end":116.14,"text":"In Barcelona, the Sagrada Familia is a Catholic church designed by Antoni Gaudi."},{"start":117,"end":121.56,"text":"It is the tallest church in the world, and parts of it are a UNESCO World Heritage Site."},{"start":122.66,"end":128.22,"text":"In Granada, Andalusia, the Alhambra brings us back to Al-Andalus."},{"start":128.22,"end":132.44,"text":"This old palace and fortress is a famous example of Islamic building design."},{"start":133.4,"end":138.1,"text":"In central Madrid, the Museo del Prado is Spain’s main national art museum."},{"start":138.1,"end":145.48,"text":"It opened in 1819 and has many paintings by Francisco Goya and Diego Velazquez."},{"start":145.48,"end":150.86,"text":"These places offer different ways to explore Spain: through a church, a palace, or art."},{"start":151.94,"end":156.28,"text":"Lunch is usually Spain’s large main meal, starting around 2:00 to 2:30 in the afternoon."},{"start":157.02,"end":161.2,"text":"A small snack, called merienda, may come around 6:00."},{"start":161.2,"end":163.6,"text":"Dinner starts late, from about 8:30."},{"start":164.26,"end":167.98,"text":"After a meal, people may stay at the table to relax and talk."},{"start":168.46,"end":170.44,"text":"This time together is called sobremesa."},{"start":171.44,"end":173.1,"text":"Food also connects with regions."},{"start":174.08,"end":179,"text":"Paella is a Valencian rice dish from the east coast, cooked in a wide, flat pan."},{"start":179,"end":184.88,"text":"Gazpacho is an Andalusian cold vegetable soup, often made with tomato and eaten in summer."},{"start":185.86,"end":190.08,"text":"Tortilla is a thick omelette with eggs and potatoes, often with onion."},{"start":190.96,"end":193.9,"text":"Tapas are small snacks that can be hot or cold."},{"start":194.52,"end":196.46,"text":"Several tapas together can make a full meal."},{"start":197.7,"end":202.8,"text":"The Seville Fair, also called Feria de Abril, is an Andalusian fair in Seville."},{"start":203.34,"end":206.68,"text":"It usually begins two weeks after Holy Week, the week before Easter."},{"start":207.4,"end":210.28,"text":"The fair has rows of decorated tents called casetas."},{"start":210.8,"end":214.38,"text":"These belong to families, groups of friends, clubs, and other groups."},{"start":215.1,"end":221.1,"text":"From about nine at night until early morning, people dance sevillanas, a folk dance danced in pairs."},{"start":221.94,"end":225.08,"text":"Southern Spain is also the home of flamenco."},{"start":226.24,"end":230.28,"text":"Flamenco is an Andalusian art of music, song, and dance."},{"start":231.1,"end":233.62,"text":"The Romani people of Andalusia helped create it."},{"start":234.28,"end":240.3,"text":"Like Valencian paella, flamenco has a local home, even though people know it far beyond that region."}],"words":[{"text":"Spain","start":0,"end":0.34},{"text":"is","start":0.34,"end":0